config AXS15231B
	bool "AXS15231B QSPI LCD display controller driver"
	depends on DT_HAS_AXS_AXS15231B_ENABLED
	select MSPI
	help
	  Enable driver for the AXS15231B QSPI LCD controller (e.g. the 3.5"
	  320x480 panel on the Guition JC3248W535 / cobantab1a module). The panel
	  is driven over QSPI: every frame is one bus transaction whose 32-bit
	  header (command phase + address phase, 1-wire) is followed by its
	  payload - parameters on one data line, pixels on the lines the node's
	  mspi-io-mode selects (1-1-1 or 1-1-4).

	  The node must sit on an MSPI controller ("espressif,esp32-mspi"): only
	  there are header and pixels a single transfer with per-phase line widths,
	  and the controller drives the CS line. SPI cannot frame this panel.

config AXS15231B_ROTATION_HW
	bool "Rotate the panel in hardware (MADCTL MV) instead of in software"
	default n
	depends on AXS15231B
	help
	  With a non-zero `rotation` on the panel node, turn the display with
	  MADCTL's MV/mirror bits and report the swapped resolution through the
	  display API, so LVGL renders the rotated UI natively and frames stream
	  through the driver unchanged (zero per-frame cost).

	  NOT YET PROVEN on this panel's QSPI row-pointer stream: the bench
	  findings that settled the write protocol were made at MADCTL 0x00.
	  Until a test pattern confirms the stream order under MV (see the note
	  in axs15231b.c), leave this off - the default software route transposes
	  each frame in the driver and is the proven path.

